Q900 development Capsule signing

  QcFMPRoot.cer      Public DER root embedded in the XBL configuration.
  QcFMPRoot.pub.pem  Same root certificate in PEM for Capsule generation.
  QcFMPSub.pub.pem   Public intermediate certificate.
  QcFMPCert.pem      Capsule signer certificate and private key.

Keep the signing PEM out of source control and restrict file access. The
development factory build reads QcFMPRoot.cer and re-signs the Gunyah XBL
configuration in Qualcomm SecTools TEST mode. No Capsule private material is
needed to build the factory image.

For a new development setup, generate a Capsule certificate chain using the
Qualcomm procedure and install these four files locally:
https://github.com/qualcomm/cbsp-boot-utilities/tree/main/uefi_capsule_generation#3-working-of-the-host-signing-tool

Production XBL configuration signing requires the OEM signing chain trusted
by the target devices.
